  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Shengmating may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2 through multiple pathways, with the inner centromere protein acting as a common target. Shengmating is shown to have targets that include the inner centromere protein, which in turn is targeted by stilbostemin B 3'-beta-D-glucopyranoside, lehualide A, and milbemycin oxime. These compounds are likely to modulate the activity of the inner centromere protein, which is ultimately targeted by the kinase CDC2L2. The scores from the three paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with the highest score attributed to stilbostemin B 3'-beta-D-glucopyranoside. The overlapping targets suggest that Shengmating may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the inner centromere protein, which is a key regulatory node in cellular processes. The evidence supports a potential role for Shengmating in modulating the activity of the CDC2L2 kinase, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
